Ported components:
  - scripts/router_core.py  ← preset/router-standard/router-core.mjs
    (task-classification regexes, behavior bands, personas, complexity
    heuristic, mode parsing — preserved verbatim where they are the measured
    artifacts of the upstream P1-P23 experiments)
  - scripts/delivery_check.py  ← the deliveryCheck gate in
    preset/router-standard/router-bootstrap-v34.mjs (v1.23-v1.28 semantics:
    file/utf8 checks + 8-kind evidence manifest, reviewed visuals,
    non-blocking numeric hint), re-exposed as a CLI
  - skills/mode-router/SKILL.md  ← the v1.20 four-stage progressive workflow
    (understanding→planning→development→verification, completion-signal
    advancement, STAGE_GUIDES behavioral guidance) as a protocol

Note on design lineage: v1.20 (read in full from router-bootstrap-v34.mjs)
fixes the persona to a single RL sentence and enforces behavior via staged
tool disclosure; the older band-swapped-persona design lives on only as
informational mode output. This port follows the v1.20 mainline.

Not ported (DSH-runtime specific, no ZCode equivalent):
  - injector/ (runtime agent-loop injection, dev_* tooling, restrict)
  - phase_begin/phase_advance/tools_catalog secondary disclosure plumbing
  - graded/ (separate two-tier task-protocol plugin)

Measured claims (three behavior bands, weak-persona optima per model,
completion-signal advancement, anchor effects) originate from the upstream
repository's P1-P23 experiments on DeepSeek models and are cited, not
re-verified here.
